The survey's leads are mostly noise, and the traces point to a single fault. Here is the conclusion.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "geo",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6 med_ms, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 3,1",
          "claim": "Search's geo.Geo/Nearby client spans take about 1.6 s median (p95 ~3 s), while geo's server spans stay at about 0.14 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT src, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6 med_ms, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM (SELECT 'abn' src, * FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', * FROM normal_traces) WHERE span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4 ORDER BY 2,4,1",
          "claim": "Normal period: search→geo client median about 0.46 ms; the abnormal client spans are roughly 3,500 times slower, with geo server time unchanged."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, metric, sum(CASE WHEN src='abn' THEN value END)/NULLIF(sum(CASE WHEN src='abn' THEN 1 END),0) abn_avg, sum(CASE WHEN src='norm' THEN value END)/NULLIF(sum(CASE WHEN src='norm' THEN 1 END),0) norm_avg FROM (SELECT 'abn' src, * FROM abnormal_metrics_sum UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', * FROM normal_metrics_sum) WHERE service_name IN ('search','geo') AND metric IN ('k8s.pod.network.errors','k8s.pod.network.io') GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Pod network error counters stay at zero for search and geo; no packet errors or drops, so the delay is not loss."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "geo",
      "to": "search",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='search' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Client') OR (service_name='geo' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Server') GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "The slow geo wait appears in search's client spans (p95 ~3 s) while geo's server spans remain around 0.2 ms."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels') OR (service_name='search' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Server') GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "Frontend's HTTP /hotels p95 is about 2,987 ms, matching search.Search/Nearby server p95 of about 2,981 ms; no errors on either."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

